Package: bayr
Type: Package
Title: Tidy and Unified Reporting of Bayesian Regression Models
Version: 0.9.8
Authors@R: 
    person("Martin", "Schmettow", email = "schmettow@web.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a unified, tidy interface for reporting Bayesian
    regression models in the spirit of the Bayesian New Statistics (Kruschke
    and Liddell, 2018, <doi:10.1177/2515245918771329>). Wrapper functions
    extract parameter estimates and posterior distributions from 'brms' and
    'rstanarm' models, and tidy summaries from 'lme4' fits, into a common long
    format, so that customized tables and plots can be built with tidy
    processing chains. Methods for coefficients, predictions and information
    criteria make it easy to produce publication-ready output in
    'knitr'/'Markdown' reports.
